@startuml auth-session
!include common.iuml
left to right direction
title Login or create, 1 derivation either way

actor Browser
component "Server\nusername validation" as server
database "Store" as store
component "User missing\nfresh salt, argon2id derive\nwith the current parameters,\ncreate the user if absent" as missing
component "User exists\nargon2id derive with the stored\nper user parameters,\nconstant time compare" as exists
component "Session\ncrypto random token, TTL in hours,\nrequests carry the token,\nauthenticate by session" as session
rectangle "Bad credentials" as bad #F8DFE6

Browser --> server : Username and password
server --> store : Look up the user
store --> missing
store --> exists
missing --> session
exists --> session
exists --> bad : The compare fails
session --> Browser : Session cookie
bad --> Browser : Rejected
note bottom of server
  Both paths run exactly 1 argon2id derivation,
  so timing does not reveal whether the account exists
end note
note bottom of store
  The seeded admin account is verified at boot,
  a foreign row holding the admin name warns
  instead of logging in
end note
@enduml
